    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** (74.65) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.23) serving as our primary engines for offensive production. **Corbin Carroll** remains the high-water mark; while he faces a competent arm in Kevin Gausman, his elite sprint speed against a pitcher with a slow delivery provides an immediate ceiling for stolen bases, netting him a +4% bump on his already strong base projection. **Seiya Suzuki** draws a similarly favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly, whose 5.27 xERA invites aggression. The combination of **Seiya Suzuki** batting second and benefiting from a +19% SP skill adjustment makes him our most efficient bet for run production today.\n\nDown the order, we are capitalizing on specific environmental and profile edges. **Max Muncy** (61.65) sneaks into the \"Strong\" category thanks to an advantageous park factor (+10%) and his utility against Zebby Matthews, while **Mickey Moniak** (57.96) benefits from a +14% boost due to dynamic platoon splits. We remain cautious with **Zach McKinstry** (41.67), who is currently our most fragile start; while a favorable wind blowing out provides a marginal lift, his -18% SP skill adjustment against Drew Rasmussen keeps him near the floor. **Griffin Conine** remains the most interesting bench case at 35.11; despite an impressive 0.383 xwOBA, he was squeezed out by a combination of a tough matchup against Ranger Suarez and a detrimental platoon disadvantage that limited his efficiency score below our roster threshold.\n\nFinal roster construction rests on the assumption that all lineups posted are as anticipated, though the \"Lineup Pending\" tag on **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Max Muncy**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Zach McKinstry** introduces a layer of volatility. We are monitoring **Josh Naylor** closely, as the matchup against Zack Wheeler is the toughest of the day\u2014the -19% SP skill penalty and -5% park adjustment render his 46.99 score tenuous. If these lineups shift significantly, we have no viable bench depth to pivot to given that **Trevor Story** remains on the IL and **Brice Turang** is unavailable due to an off-day. Proceed with the current configuration as the highest efficiency path toward maintaining our 5x5 standing.",
